ural advantage. It’s more aggressive than simply developing a piece, and the d4 square is currently unguarded by White pawns (their pawns are still on the second rank). The knight on c3 has to move, and if it moves, Black can follow up with Bg4 or Nf6 with strong pressure.\n\n**Answer:** P: d5-d4'}
